From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:58:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo: load the ADSP
 firmware from the phone

Name the audio DSP's split firmware (adsp.mdt + adsp.bNN) as it is stored on the phone's own
modem_a partition, like the modem, sensor and compute DSPs already do, instead of a converted
adsp.mbn that had to be built on a PC and carried in the initramfs. The partition is mounted by
userspace, after the kernel's first start attempt; the initramfs starts the ADSP once the firmware
is reachable.

Tested on a Surface Duo: booted through UEFI and by ABL, the ADSP comes up at ~3.7 s and the sound
card registers; postmarketOS duo-health reports no failures.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-workbench.dtsi | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-workbench.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-workbench.dtsi
index 98aad4269..f404c0798 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-workbench.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-workbench.dtsi
@@ -289,6 +289,15 @@ &remoteproc_cdsp {
 	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8150/microsoft/cdsp.mdt";
 };
 
+/*
+ * Audio DSP: split firmware from the phone's modem_a partition (image/adsp.mdt + .bNN), like the other DSPs. It is
+ * not reachable when the kernel first tries (~0.5 s), so the initramfs links modem_a and starts the ADSP itself.
+ * Nothing proprietary has to be converted or carried in the initramfs.
+ */
+&remoteproc_adsp {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8150/microsoft/adsp.mdt";
+};
+
 /* BT UART pins (QUP SE13: gpio43 CTS, 44 RTS, 45 TX, 46 RX) — uart13 has no pinctrl in sm8150.dtsi; without these the
  * pins are never muxed and every BT command times out (2026-11-03). States copied from the SM8150-HDK WCN399x patch. */
 &tlmm {
